// Backward-compatibility read facade for kubernetesEvents (migration step 1 / PR1).
//
// Thin, cheap view inheriting the legacy table name. Legacy Kubernetes events were
// stored in two databases: service-cluster events in ServiceLogs.kubernetesEvents and
// hosted-control-plane events in HostedControlPlaneLogs.kubernetesEvents. The facade
// unions the new routed table (tab_kubernetesEvents) with both legacy sources so no
// historical events are lost during the migration. Legacy data ages out by retention.
//
// union kind=outer tolerates minor column drift between the sources.
// skipvalidation is required because the cross-database sources are not resolvable
// at script-execution time (validation emulator, single-database deploy).
.create-or-alter function with (view = true, skipvalidation = "true", docstring = "compat view: kubernetesEvents (new tab_kubernetesEvents + legacy ServiceLogs + HostedControlPlaneLogs)", folder = "views")
kubernetesEvents() {
    union kind=outer
      database("AllAroHcpLogs").tab_kubernetesEvents,
      database("ServiceLogs").kubernetesEvents,
      database("HostedControlPlaneLogs").kubernetesEvents
}
